{"unit_id": "script_0004", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 4}, "text": "The world is multimodal:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0005", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 5}, "text": "Ultimate goal: **omni model**", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0006", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 6}, "text": "- Input any combination of modalities (understanding)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0007", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 7}, "text": "- Output any combination of modalities (generation)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0008", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 8}, "text": "Where we are today:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0009", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 9}, "text": "- Transformers work really well. So we gotta use them.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0010", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 10}, "text": "- Transformers speak tokens (discrete or continuous), where a token represents some ~semantic unit of information.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0011", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 11}, "text": "- Therefore, we must convert everything into tokens.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0012", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 12}, "text": "- Note: we had to do this with text (recall the tokenization lecture).", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0013", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 13}, "text": "- For non-text modalities, this is more challenging...", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0014", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 14}, "text": "Questions:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0015", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 15}, "text": "1. How do we input non-text data (e.g., understand images)?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0016", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 16}, "text": "2. How do we output non-text data (e.g., generate audio)?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0017", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 17}, "text": "Summary:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0018", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 18}, "text": "- Frontier models are expected to be multimodal (natively multimodal, omni)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0019", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 19}, "text": "- Fundamental challenge: how to encode non-text modalities?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0020", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 20}, "text": "- Comprehension and generation might demand different things (semantics versus finer-grained details)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0021", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 21}, "text": "- Balance images + video (lower information density) and text for training stability", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0022", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 22}, "text": "- Continuous encoders + Transformer + diffusion models for generation", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0023", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 23}, "text": "Context:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0024", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 24}, "text": "- Computer vision models were trained on annotated images.", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0025", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 25}, "text": "- Question: is it possible to leverage the much larger amount of (image, caption) pairs?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0026", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 26}, "text": "Method:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0027", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 27}, "text": "- Get a batch of (image, text) examples (e.g., 32768)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0028", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 28}, "text": "- Encode each image and each text", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0029", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 29}, "text": "- For each image, prefer its aligned text over other texts", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0030", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 30}, "text": "- For each text, prefer its aligned image over other images", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0031", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 31}, "text": "Data:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0032", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 32}, "text": "- Searched for 500K queries, get ~20K (image, text) pairs per query", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0033", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 33}, "text": "- Trained on 400M image-text pairs", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0034", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 34}, "text": "- Didn't release the dataset", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0035", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 35}, "text": "- Images come in all resolutions (arbitrary W x H)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0036", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 36}, "text": "- Resize using bicubic interpolation so shorter side is 336 pixels", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0037", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 37}, "text": "- Center crop (cuts off borders to get 336 x 336)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0038", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 38}, "text": "Vision encoder:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0039", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 39}, "text": "- Attention pooling: do QKV with query = global average of activations", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0040", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 40}, "text": "- Best model: ViT-L/14@336px (L = large, 14x14 patches, 3 channels, trained on 336x336 resolution images)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0041", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 41}, "text": "Text encoder:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0042", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 42}, "text": "- GPT-2 Transformer (63M parameters, 12 layers)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0043", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 43}, "text": "- Encode [BOS] ... [EOS], return [EOS] activation at highest layer", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0044", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 44}, "text": "Headline result:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0045", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 45}, "text": "- On ImageNet, zero-shot CLIP outperformed ResNet-50 trained on 1.2M ImageNet images", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0046", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 46}, "text": "Ablation:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0047", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 47}, "text": "- Alternative: predict text from images directly", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0048", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 48}, "text": "- Much less compute efficient compared to CLIP-style ranking", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0049", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 49}, "text": "Summary:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0050", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 50}, "text": "- Encoding of images captures semantics given by (noisy) text", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0051", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 51}, "text": "- Design decisions chosen based on image classification (not very fine-grained)", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0052", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 52}, "text": "- Technical: requires large batch sizes, softmax operation over full batch", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0053", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 53}, "text": "Objective:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0054", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 54}, "text": "- CLIP: multiclass classification for (text, image) versus (text, image') for all image'", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0055", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 55}, "text": "- SigLIP: binary classification for (text, image) - aligned or not?", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0056", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 56}, "text": "Data:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0057", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 57}, "text": "- Scraped from the Internet", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0058", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 58}, "text": "- Used automatic OCR to extract text from images", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0059", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 59}, "text": "- Keep 10% highest quality", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0060", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 60}, "text": "- Supports 100 languages", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0061", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 61}, "text": "Efficiency:", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
{"unit_id": "script_0062", "source_type": "official_executable_lecture_block", "source_id": "lecture_17.py", "loc": {"block": 62}, "text": "- CLIP: 10 days on 256 TPUv3", "asset_path": null, "required": true}
